---

The shortest splitline method, and the published maps this project reproduces
and extends, come from the Center for Range Voting. Their page
https://www.rangevoting.org/SplitLR.html states:

    We give permission to all to re-use these images provided they cite the
    Center for Range Voting, this web page, and us; the Shortest Splitline
    algorithm was invented by Warren D. Smith and the program that produced
    the images was written by Ivan Ryan; the underlying data is from the US
    Census Bureau.

Accordingly, and for the maps generated here as much as for theirs:

    Shortest Splitline algorithm invented by Warren D. Smith.
    Original implementation by Ivan Ryan.
    Published maps and method: Center for Range Voting,
    https://www.rangevoting.org/SplitLR.html
    Underlying data: US Census Bureau.

Any reuse of images or maps from this repository should carry that credit.

